active, direct evidence of diet-induced microbiome changes driving ICI efficacy in humans requires further interventional trials with paired microbiome-clinical outcome data.\n\n    Check against constraints:\n    - No overgeneralization.\n    - Distinguishes findings.\n    - Explains meaning without repeating numbers.\n    - Matches decision logic.\n\n4.  **Determine `decision`, `still_missing`, `read_focus`, `external_ask`, `reason`:**\n    - `decision`: `external_research` (The core question asks for direct confirmation in human cohorts. Materials show feasibility and FMT-based inference, but explicitly lack human microbiome-efficacy linkage data.)\n    - `still_missing`: 人类饮食干预队列中同步报告的、与ICI临床疗效（如ORR/PFS/OS）直接关联的具体微生物组组成变化数据（如特定菌属/菌株丰度与疗效的相关性分析）。\n    - `read_focus`: 需检索DIET试验及BEWELL研究的全文或后续发表文献，确认是否包含人类受试者基线与干预后的宏基因组/16S测序数据及其与肿瘤缓解率或生存期的相关性分析。\n    - `external_ask`: 检索“dietary intervention human ICI trial microbiome composition clinical outcome correlation”或“DIET trial NCT04645680 full text microbiome sequencing”，寻找同时报告人类饮食干预前后肠道菌群演变与ICI治疗应答（如RECIST标准评估）的原始研究或注册更新。\n    - `reason`: 现有材料仅证实了饮食干预可改变人类外周免疫表型及肠道菌群结构（如毛螺菌科富集），并通过人源小鼠FMT模型间接提示菌群介导的ICI疗效提升潜力；但摘要明确说明人类队列本身未提供具体的微生物组成分变化与疗效因果链条的直接数据，疗效验证依赖于临床前模型，尚未满足“人类队列中直接证实”的成功标准。\n\n5.  **Final Review against Constraints:**\n    - `quantitative_comparisons` first? Yes.\n    - Format matches? Yes.\n    - `usable_content` reads well, focuses on specific findings, distinguishes studies, explains conditions, avoids overclaiming causality? Yes.\n    - `decision` correctly assesses if the *specific question* is solved? Yes, `external_research`.\n    - Numbers handled correctly? Yes, grouped per metric/group as instructed.\n    - No automatic causal claims? Explicitly stated FMT inference vs direct human data.\n    - JSON structure correct? Will ensure strict compliance.\n    - One minor adjustment: The prompt says `groups 是 [{group:原文组名或缩写,value:紧邻该组的结果含单位}]`. I will make sure the values are exactly as reported. For p-valu